Cell["The If condition can be in one of the three forms:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(If[test, \ then]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(If[test, \ then, \ else]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(If[test, \ then, \ else, \ unknown]\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Where \"test\" is an expression which evaluates to the symbol True or False; \
if test evaluates to True, the \"then'' expression is evaluated, otherwise, \
if it is False, the \"else'' expression is evaluated.  If test is an \
expression other than True or False, unknown part will be evaluated. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(If[True, \ a, \ b, \ c]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(a\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Logical expressions can be formed similar to C:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    RowBox[{"<", "                   ", 
      StyleBox[\(less\ than\),
        FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"<=", " ", 
      RowBox[{\(( \[LessEqual] )\), "      ", 
        StyleBox["less",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox[" ",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox["equal",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{">", "                   ", 
      StyleBox[\(greater\ than\),
        FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{">=", "  ", 
      RowBox[{\(( \[GreaterEqual] )\), "     ", 
        StyleBox["greater",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox[" ",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox["equal",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Equal]", "                  ", 
      StyleBox["equal",
        FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"!=", " ", 
      RowBox[{\(( \[NotEqual] \ )\), "     ", 
        StyleBox["not",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox[" ",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
        StyleBox["equal",
          FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
      RowBox[{"&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{\(( \[And] )\), "     ", 
          StyleBox["AND",
            FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
      RowBox[{"||", " ", 
        RowBox[{\(( \[Or] )\), "     ", 
          StyleBox["OR",
            FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"===", "              ", 
      StyleBox["identical",
        FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1],
        Background->None]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"=!=", "              ", 
      StyleBox[\(not\ identical\),
        FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]}]}], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Within the notebook interface, we can also use equivalent math symbols: e.g.:\
\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(x = 4; 
    If[x\  \[NotEqual] \ 0\  \[And] \ x\  > \ 2, \ Print[x]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(4\)], "Print"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The last two (===,=!=) is a stronger form of equal or not equal:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \({a \[Equal] b, \ a === b}\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({a == b, False}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\((1 + x)\)^2\  == \ 1\  + \ 2  x\  + \ x^2\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(True\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Typing of special symbols", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Special symbol like \[Pi] or \[Alpha] can be typed in \n\t(1) using \
palettes (File \[Rule] Palates \[Rule] BasicInput),\n\t(2) key strokes with \
ESC code ESC.  e.g. \[Pi] is ESC p ESC, or ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"T", 
          AdjustmentBox["E",
            BoxMargins->{{-0.075, -0.085}, {0, 0}},
            BoxBaselineShift->0.5], "X"}]]]],
  " style input ESC \\pi ESC.\nSuperscripts/subscripts can be typed in with \
Ctrl-^, Ctrl-_; Control space back to normal.  e.g.  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\_2. \)]],
  " By Ctrl-@ we get the square root symbol ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\@\[Placeholder]\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\((1\  + \ \[Alpha]\ )\)\^2\  // \ Expand\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(1 + 2\ \[Alpha] + \[Alpha]\^2\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(N[\[Pi]]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(3.141592653589793`\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Programming example: Gaussian elimination", "Subtitle"],

Cell["\<\
1. What user interface to use?
2. How much to check the validity of input data?
3. Error handling, what to do if solution does not exist? \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We shall do a simple-minded Gaussian elimination with row pivoting.   \
Given the matrix A and vector b which forms the linear system:\nA = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      TagBox[
        RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
              {\(a\_\(1, 1\)\), \(a\_\(1, 2\)\), "...", \(a\_\(1, n\)\)},
              {\(a\_\(2, 1\)\), \(a\_\(2, 2\)\), "...", \(a\_\(2, n\)\)},
              {"...", "...", "...", "..."},
              {\(a\_\(m, 1\)\), \(a\_\(m, 2\)\), \(a\_\(m, 3\)\), \(a\_\(m, 
                    n\)\)}
              }], ")"}],
        Function[ BoxForm`e$, 
          MatrixForm[ BoxForm`e$]]]]],
  "       b = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      TagBox[
        RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
              {\(b\_1\)},
              {\(b\_2\)},
              {"."},
              {\(b\_m\)}
              }], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
        Function[ BoxForm`e$, 
          MatrixForm[ BoxForm`e$]]]]],
  "\nwe combine A and b into a single matrix M = [A, b].  At step i, we are \
at the diagonal element ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_ii\)]],
  " and the matrix M looks like\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      TagBox[
        RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
              {\(a\_\(1, 1\)\), \(a\_\(1, 2\)\), \(a\_\(1, 3\)\), \(a\_\(1, 
                    4\)\), \(b\_1\)},
              {
                "0", \(a\_\(2, 2\)\), \(a\_\(2, 3\)\), \(a\_\(2, 
                    4\)\), \(b\_2\)},
              {"0", "0", 
                StyleBox[\(a\_\(i, i\)\),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
                StyleBox[\(a\_\(3, 4\)\),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
                StyleBox[\(\(b\_i\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)
                  \),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]},
              {"0", "0", 
                StyleBox[\(a\_\(j, i\)\),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
                StyleBox[\(a\_\(j, 4\)\),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]], 
                StyleBox[\(b\_\(\(j\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)
                      \)\),
                  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0, 1]]},
              {"0", "0", \(a\_\(m, i\)\), \(a\_\(m, 4\)\), \(b\_m\)}
              }], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
        Function[ BoxForm`e$, 
          MatrixForm[ BoxForm`e$]]]]],
  "\nWe multiply ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_ii\)]],
  " to equation j (jth row) and multiply current equation i (ith-row) by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_ji\)]],
  ", then subtract.  The result will be our new row j."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(gauss[a_List, \ b_List]\  := \ 
      Module[\ {m = a, nrow, \ ncol, i, j, c0, c1, \ 
          new}, \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] (*\ 
          We\ comment\ in\ code\ with\ parenthsis\ star\ pair\ \
*) \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] (*\(\(*\)\(\ \)\(first\)\(\ \
\)\(we\)\(\ \)\(combine\)\(\ \)\(a\)\(\ \)\(with\)\(\ \)\(b\)\), \ 
          by\ tranposing\ trice\ **) \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine]m\ \
 = \ Transpose[m]\ ~Join~{\ b}; \[IndentingNewLine]m\  = \ 
          Transpose[m]; \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] (*\ 
          We\ don' t\ have\ to\ pass\ the\ matrix\ size\ explicitly, \ 
          the\ length\ of\ the\ list\ will\ tell\ us\ the\ number\ of\ rows\ \
n\ *) \ \[IndentingNewLine]nrow\  = \ 
          Length[a]; \[IndentingNewLine]ncol\  = \ 
          Length[a[\([1]\)]]; \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] (*\ 
          Run\ along\ the\ diagonal\ \
*) \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine]For[i\  = \ 1, \ 
          i\  <= \ Min[nrow, \ 
              ncol], \ \(++i\), \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine] (*\ 
            Do\ a\ swap\ equation\ if\ diagonal\ term\ a\_ii\ is\ zero\ \
*) \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine]If[
            m[\([i, i]\)]\  === \ 0, \[IndentingNewLine]For[
              j\  = \ i\  + \ 1, \ 
              j\  \[LessEqual] \ nrow, \ \(++j\), \[IndentingNewLine]If[
                m[\([j, i]\)]\  =!= \ 
                  0, \[IndentingNewLine]{m[\([i]\)], \ 
                    m[\([j]\)]}\  = \ {m[\([j]\)], \ m[\([i]\)]}; \ 
                Break[]]]\ , \ \[IndentingNewLine]]; \[IndentingNewLine]\
\[IndentingNewLine]c0\  = \ m[\([i, i]\)]; \[IndentingNewLine]For[
            j\  = \ i + 1, \ 
            j\  \[LessEqual] \ nrow, \ \(++j\), \[IndentingNewLine]\ 
            c1\  = \ m[\([j, i]\)]; \[IndentingNewLine]new\  = \ \ c0\ *\ 
                  m[\([j]\)]\  - \ 
                c1\ *\ m[\([i]\)]; \[IndentingNewLine]m[\([j]\)]\  = \ 
              Simplify\  /@ \ 
                new;\[IndentingNewLine]]; \[IndentingNewLine]\
\[IndentingNewLine] (*\ 
            We\ printing\ out\ at\ intermediate\ step\ for\ debuging\ \
*) \[IndentingNewLine]\[IndentingNewLine]\ 
          Print[MatrixForm[
              m]]\[IndentingNewLine]]; \
\[IndentingNewLine]m\[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["Here are some testing runs:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(gauss[{{a, b}, {c, d}}, {1, 2}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(gauss[Table[a[i, j], {i, 1, 3}, {j, 1, 3}], 
      Table[b[i], {i, 1, 3}]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["backsub[] will be left for the next lab problem. ", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Reading for this Lecture

1.7 (simple programs)
2.5.8 to 2.5.9 (flow controls)\
\>", "Subtitle"]
},
